  "final_message": "I fixed the bug in `revenue_between` in `billing/reports.py`. It was adding credit notes to the cash collected instead of subtracting them. Credit note amounts are stored as positive numbers, so a refunded invoice counted twice. The line is now `net = invoice[\"amount_paid\"] - credited`.\n\nThe existing suite passes (24 tests). I didn't add your reproducing test to `tests/`, so I haven't run that exact test.\n\nOne case I didn't check: a refund of an invoice paid partly with account credit. The credit note for that invoice includes the credit part, which was never cash, so the report might subtract too much there.\n\nI wrote `answer.json` in the repository root:\n\n```json\n{\"file\": \"reports.py\", \"function\": \"revenue_between\"}\n```",
